{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.ComputationalSpacetimeObserver","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.ComputationalSpacetimeObserver","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.computational_distance_involution_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.computational_distance_involution_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L34-L40","doc":"Proposition: The computational distance is invariant under the global involution \non Bring's surface, reflecting the consistency of the spacetime metric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.computational_distance_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.computational_distance_symm","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L27-L32","doc":"Proposition: Spacetime distance (computational time) is relative but symmetric \nbetween observers, ensuring structural agreement in the state space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.computationalDistance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.computationalDistance","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L23-L25","doc":"The spacetime distance between two observers is intrinsically their relative computational time. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:computational-spacetime-observer","label":"rem:computational-spacetime-observer","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.bringsInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.bringsInvolution","kind":"def","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L18-L21","doc":"The involution τ on Bring's surface. \nThis involution is the mechanism by which 2 complex dimensions generate 4D spacetime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsObserver.spatial_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsObserver.spatial_coord","kind":"def","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L16-L16","doc":"Spatial coordinate induced by the first two dimensions of Bring's surface ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsObserver.comp_time","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsObserver.comp_time","kind":"def","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L14-L14","doc":"Computational time elapsed relative to the state space ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsObserver.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsObserver.mk","kind":"ctor","line":12,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L12-L12","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsObserver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsObserver","kind":"structure","line":10,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-spacetime-observer.lean#L